================================================================================
The repo HEAD (c9c6fdb9, merge P-0237-AiUsageCard) is RED before this surface is touched. None of
the following is caused by AnimatedMarker (grep of the 1829-error full-app build: 0 errors in
shared-surfaces/AnimatedMarker). Handling is documented so nothing is silently worked around.

A. FULL-APP iOS/macOS BUILD -- BLOCKED-PREEXISTING (out of scope).
   $ xcodebuild -scheme TeslaSync -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 16' build test
      -> ** BUILD FAILED **   IOS_EXIT=65
   1829 compile errors, attributed by directory:
        559  TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets
        191  TeslaSync/feature-views
         23  Sources/DashboardWidgets
          0  TeslaSync/shared-surfaces      <-- this surface is clean
   Root cause: hundreds of independently-generated sibling surfaces each redeclare the SAME
   public types in the single app module, e.g. `public struct DashboardWidgetSize` is defined
   15+ times (DigitalTwinWidget.Model, MotorHistoryWidget.Model, OdometerCounterWidget.Projection,
   ... + twice in Sources/DashboardWidgets), and `VehicleHeroModel/Projection/Connection/...` are
   likewise multiply-defined -> "'DashboardWidgetSize' is ambiguous for type lookup" (152x),
   "'VehicleHeroModel' is ambiguous" (149x), cascading "cannot infer key path / contextual base"
   (720x+). Deduplicating these belongs to those surfaces' owners ("Other surfaces in the same
   feature ... Out of Scope" per this prompt) and would touch hundreds of unrelated files. NOT
   attempted. The AnimatedMarker surface is proven correct by the focused build+test above.
   FULL_APP_BUILD=BLOCKED-PREEXISTING-OUT-OF-SCOPE (0 errors attributable to this surface)

B. App-target test-file leak -- FIXED (wiring only, required for the app target to even link).
   HEAD's project.yml includes `TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets` + `TeslaSync/feature-views` in the
   iOS+macOS APP targets with NO excludes, so ~247 co-located *Tests.swift files compile into the
   app target and fail `import XCTest` ("unable to resolve module dependency: 'XCTest'"). These
   test files were never in any test target (Tests/Unit only) so they never ran -- they only broke
   the app build. Fix: add `excludes: ["*Tests.swift"]` to those two paths (and shared-surfaces)
   in both app targets -- the same structure used for the new surface. Status quo preserved (those
   tests were not running before and are not wired to run now); the app target stops ingesting test
   code. This unblocks compilation far enough to reveal defect (A).

C. swiftlint --strict -- FIXED 1 pre-existing violation (shared host gate).
   TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/LifetimeStatsWidget.Adapter.swift: project() spanned 78 lines
   (function_body_length, error under --strict). Behaviour-preserving extraction into
   coreStats(...) + wideStats(...) private helpers. No logic change.

D. swiftformat --lint -- FIXED 1 pre-existing violation (shared host gate).
   TeslaSync/feature-views/ActionBuilder.Previews.swift:48 missing blank line before a declaration
   (blankLinesBetweenScopes). Auto-fixed by swiftformat (one blank line). No logic change.

